rag-tag and bob-tail, of scullions and loafers in Paris during a time of political excitement. He met a friend, who was dumbfounded at the gentleman's' ridiculous and incomprehensible conduct. He said to him :
' Why, what are you doing here ? Why do you follow these people ' ? The gentleman answered : ' Do not attempt to stop me ;
I am their leader ; I have to follow them/ The hon. gentleman (Mr. R. L Borden) is the leader, I am sorry to say, of the mean and despicable creatures who are seeking to wrest that word from its proper connection and give it a meaning which it cannot properly bear.
